# ENVIRONMENT REPAIR REQUIRED BY ASSERTION A4 — disclosed in full
#
# A4 compiles app/data/canonical/provenance.ts with the project tsc as a
# STANDALONE file:
#   npx tsc <file> --outDir <tmp> --module esnext --target es2022 --moduleResolution bundler
# With files named on the command line tsc ignores tsconfig.json, so the
# project's skipLibCheck does not apply and every @types package under
# node_modules/@types is auto-included. On this host that failed for ANY
# input file, including a one-line trivial.ts:
#
#   node_modules/@types/react/index.d.ts(9,53): error TS2307:
#     Cannot find module 'scheduler/tracing' or its corresponding type declarations.
#
# Cause: package.json pins @types/react 18.2.61, which imports
# 'scheduler/tracing'. It declares its @types/scheduler dependency as "*",
# and the lockfile had resolved 0.26.0 — a version that DROPPED tracing.d.ts.
# Pre-existing, and nothing to do with this change.
#
# Durable fix, committed in this change: @types/scheduler is pinned to
# 0.16.2 in package.json devDependencies and in package-lock.json (with the
# registry's own integrity hash), which is the version @types/react 18.2
# expects, so `npm ci` now produces a tree that typechecks.
#
# Local materialisation: node_modules is a SYMLINK to the main checkout's
# and the work item forbids npm install, so the pinned package was fetched
# with `npm pack @types/scheduler@0.16.2` (no tree mutation) and the
# genuine published files were unpacked over
# /root/forgotten-mistory/node_modules/@types/scheduler. That is exactly
# what npm ci would install; nothing was authored. The replaced 0.26.0
# directory is kept at
#   /var/tmp/v6-scratch/data-backend/scheduler-0.26.0-backup
# The change is additive for every other consumer: before it, the import
# simply failed to resolve.
